<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

  <title>Recommended Data Sources</title>

  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      max-width: 1000px;
      margin: 40px auto;
      padding: 20px;
      background: #f5f5f5;
      color: #222;
    }

    h1 {
      text-align: center;
    }

    h2 {
      margin-top: 40px;
      border-bottom: 2px solid #333;
      padding-bottom: 8px;
    }

    .resource {
      background: white;
      padding: 16px;
      margin: 12px 0;
      border-radius: 8px;
      border: 1px solid #ddd;
    }

    .resource a {
      font-size: 18px;
      font-weight: bold;
      color: #0056b3;
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    .resource a:hover {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .resource p {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>

  <h1>Recommended Data Sources</h1>

  <p>
    This page contains recommended sources for finding datasets
    for data visualization and research projects.
  </p>

  <h2>Government Data</h2>

  <div class="resource">
    <a href="https://data.gov/" target="_blank">
      Data.gov
    </a>

    <p>
      The U.S. government's central open-data portal.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="resource">
    <a href="https://www.census.gov/data.html" target="_blank">
      U.S. Census Bureau
    </a>

    <p>
      Population, demographic, economic, housing, and geographic data.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Economic Data</h2>

  <div class="resource">
    <a href="https://fred.stlouisfed.org/" target="_blank">
      FRED
    </a>

    <p>
      Economic data maintained by the Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Health Data</h2>

  <div class="resource">
    <a href="https://data.cdc.gov/" target="_blank">
      CDC Data
    </a>

    <p>
      Public health datasets from the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention.
    </p>
  </div>

</body>
</html>
